{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The IvorGeneralMIDI framework provides the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/midi.org\/general-midi","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and General MIDI 2 sound sets as Swift","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"enumerations. For General MIDI 1: the 128 instruments that a program change","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"selects, the 16 instrument families they fall into, and the 47 sounds of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"percussion key map. For General MIDI 2: the 256 instruments that a bank select","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and program change select, the 9 drum sets, and the 61 sounds of the extended","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"percussion key map. Each sound can be looked up by its program, bank, or note,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or by its name as the specification gives it, and converted back again.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Programs, notes, and channels use the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/eBardX\/IvorMIDI","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" data value types, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/documentation\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/GMMessage","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" covers the system exclusive messages that turn General MIDI on and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"off, and the General MIDI 2 effects and controllers.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import IvorGeneralMIDI","","let guitar = GM1Instrument(program: 25)","","guitar              \/\/ .acousticGuitarNylon","guitar.name         \/\/ \"Acoustic Guitar (nylon)\"","guitar.family       \/\/ .guitar","","\/\/ Name lookup ignores case and extra whitespace.","let snare = GM1PercussionSound(name: \"acoustic snare\")","","snare?.note         \/\/ 38","GM1PercussionSound.channel  \/\/ 10","","\/\/ A General MIDI 2 variation falls back to its General MIDI 1 instrument.","let ukulele = GM2Instrument(bankLSB: 1, program: 25)","","ukulele?.name           \/\/ \"Ukulele\"","ukulele?.gm1Instrument  \/\/ .acousticGuitarNylon","GM2Instrument.bankMSB   \/\/ 121","","\/\/ Bank select MSB 121, bank select LSB 1, then program change 25.","let messages = ukulele?.selectionMessages(channel: 1)","","GMMessage(content: .gm2SystemOn).systemMessage  \/\/ F0 7E 7F 09 03 F7"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/documentation\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/UsingIvorGeneralMIDI","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for a full guide to the instruments, drum sets,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"percussion sounds, and General MIDI 2 effects and controllers.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/documentation\/IvorGeneralMIDI","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/documentation\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/UsingIvorGeneralMIDI"],"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides"},{"anchor":"Messages","title":"Messages","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/documentation\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/GMMessage"]},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/documentation\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/GM1Instrument","doc:\/\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/documentation\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/GM1InstrumentFamily","doc:\/\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/documentation\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/GM1PercussionSound"],"anchor":"General-MIDI-1","title":"General MIDI 1"},{"anchor":"General-MIDI-2","title":"General MIDI 2","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/documentation\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/GM2Instrument","doc:\/\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/documentation\/IvorGeneralMIDI\/GM2DrumSet"